    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "During the Civil War, Fordoche hosted two battles, including the 1863 Fordoche Bridge fight and the 1864 Skirmish on Bayou Fordoche Road.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fordoche%2C_Louisiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fordoche’s first post office opened in 1854, with Thomas Farrar as its inaugural postmaster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fordoche%2C_Louisiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Fordoche is the newest incorporated community in Pointe Coupee Parish, becoming a town in 1994 after village status in 1961.",
